id: pm-dilou2
title: "Exporter artifact-channel contract: clean stdout, bounded receipts, and binary-safe streaming"
description: "GitHub issue #1049 demonstrates that registered exporters can write an artifact to stdout while the host appends a second generic receipt to the same stream, producing invalid structured output and duplicating the full artifact. Define an SDK-owned artifact-channel contract that lets extensions declare stdout or file delivery, suppresses incompatible host rendering by construction, preserves human summaries on a separate channel when requested, and proves JSON, CSV, opaque bytes, file output, and global JSON behavior through real extension dispatch."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[8]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:extensions","area:sdk","github:1049",output-contract,streaming,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-17T05:51:23.890Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-17T07:37:55.369Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-17T07:37:20.572Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-17T07:37:20.572Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Exporter registration metadata declares the artifact channel and receipt policy through public SDK types; A stdout artifact is the only document written to stdout by default and is never duplicated inside a generic receipt; JSON, CSV, opaque byte, file-output, human-summary, and global --json modes have explicit non-overlapping channel behavior; Derived exporter help and SDK authoring documentation expose the stream contract and compatibility behavior; Temporary installed-extension acceptance proves jq-safe and redirect-safe output"
parent: pm-mav1ak
resolution: Exporter registrations now declare stdout or file delivery plus suppress or render receipt behavior; stdout defaults to host-receipt suppression and help/inventory expose the contract.
expected_result: "Exporter artifacts remain valid and non-duplicated across JSON, CSV, opaque bytes, file output, human summaries, and global JSON mode."
actual_result: "Unit and installed-extension integration evidence proves every requested channel behavior, with exact repository coverage and packed-install acceptance."
